			"type": "text",
			"text": "Burrinjucosteus was a placoderm discovered in Wee Jasper reef in New South Wales, Australia; dating back to the Devonian. Its name is a reference to the village community of Burrinjuck, which is derived from the Aboriginal word meaning 'mountain with a rugged top' added with the Greek word for bone. It is known from parts of its skull and armor, suggesting it was a large but flat fish. It was big for its clade, growing around a meter long"
